WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.352
After Liu Bei's death, Meng Huo of the south rose in rebellion. Zhuge Liang decided to lead the army south himself.

00:00:05.702 --> 00:00:08.774
In the south the mountains were high and the forests dense, and the journey was very hard.

00:00:09.124 --> 00:00:12.316
The Shu army won victory after victory, and soon captured Meng Huo.

00:00:12.666 --> 00:00:15.666
Meng Huo was brought into the great camp, deeply unconvinced in his heart.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:21.248
But Zhuge Liang did not kill him — instead he let him go. Unconvinced, Meng Huo came back to challenge him again.

00:00:21.598 --> 00:00:24.838
Zhuge Liang smiled and said he would wait for the day Meng Huo was truly convinced.

00:00:25.188 --> 00:00:28.236
And so it went — captured and released, released and captured — seven times in all.

00:00:28.586 --> 00:00:33.506
Each time, Meng Huo thought up a new plan, but none of them succeeded.

00:00:33.856 --> 00:00:41.848
Captured the seventh time, Meng Huo was finally convinced, heart and soul. He knelt before Zhuge Liang and swore never to rebel again.

00:00:42.198 --> 00:00:45.750
Zhuge Liang helped him up with his own hands, and both men smiled.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.828
From then on, the south settled into peace, and the people of Shu Han and the south lived together in harmony.

00:00:51.178 --> 00:00:54.850
This story tells us that winning people's hearts matters even more than winning battles.

